# =============================================================================
# xrays_tissue_lead_0p1nm.mac
#
# Shielding check: a 0.1 nm (12.4 keV) X-ray pencil beam onto the layered
# chest-wall phantom with a 1 mm lead filter flush against its entrance face.
# The beam energy follows from the wavelength, E = hc/lambda with
# hc = 1239.84 eV.nm, so lambda = 0.1 nm (1 A) is a 12.398 keV photon -- a hard
# X-ray of the kind crystallography and synchrotron beamlines run on, and one
# that sits just below lead's L3 absorption edge at 13.04 keV.
#
# Detector: gdml/tissue_phantom_lead_1mm.gdml
#   - World: 60x60x60 cm (G4_AIR), phantom entrance face at z = 0
#   - Layers along z:
#      -0.1 -  0.0 cm lead filter (1 mm)
#       0.0 -  0.5 cm soft tissue (skin)
#       0.5 -  2.0 cm cortical bone (rib proxy)
#       2.0 - 12.0 cm lung
#      12.0 - 14.0 cm soft tissue
#
# Beam:
#   - Particle : gamma
#   - Energy   : monoenergetic, 12.398 keV (lambda = 0.1 nm)
#   - Position : upstream on the beam axis (z = -20 cm)
#   - Direction: along +z
#
# Expect the lead to swallow the beam whole: mu/rho ~ 76 cm2/g (interpolated
# below that edge from the NIST tables) at 11.35 g/cm3 is an attenuation length
# of ~12 um, so the 1 mm slab is ~86 of them -- a transmission of ~1e-38, with
# no primary surviving the first few tens of microns. The deposit is a sharp
# exponential right at the lead entrance face and nothing at all downstream
# (z in mm, edep in MeV):
#
#   tree->Draw("step_z>>hPb(200,-1,0)",   "step_edep");   // inside the lead
#   tree->Draw("step_z>>hTis(140,0,140)", "step_edep");   // tissue: empty
#
# For comparison, point /detector/readGDML at gdml/tissue_phantom_layered.gdml
# to get the same beam on the bare phantom, and see macros/photons_tissue_6MV.mac
# for the energies where a millimetre of lead is a perturbation, not a wall.
# =============================================================================

# --- Load geometry ---
/detector/readGDML gdml/tissue_phantom_lead_1mm.gdml

# --- Physics ---
/run/initialize

# --- Beam ---
/gun/particle    gamma
/gun/energyMode  mono
/gun/energy      12.398 keV
/gun/position    0 0 -20 cm
/gun/direction   0 0 1

# --- Run ---
/run/printProgress 500
/run/beamOn 5000
